============================================================
SHELL AND COMMAND RULES
============================================================

Use Windows PowerShell only.

Cline terminal behavior:
- Prefer VS Code Integrated Terminal mode.
- Do NOT use Background Exec mode for this project.
- The user needs to see the terminal inside VS Code.
- If Cline does not open or reuse a visible VS Code terminal, STOP and report:
  "Cline terminal is not visible. Please switch Cline Terminal Execution Mode to VS Code Integrated Terminal and Default Terminal Profile to Windows PowerShell."
- Do not continue by silently running commands in the background.

Before running any command, confirm native PowerShell session with:

Get-Location
$PSVersionTable.PSEdition
$Host.Name

Expected:
- Get-Location must work.
- $PSVersionTable.PSEdition must return Desktop or Core.
- $Host.Name should return ConsoleHost or Visual Studio Code Host.
- Prompt should start with PS.

If Get-Location is not recognized, the shell is cmd.exe or another non-PowerShell shell.

If the terminal is cmd.exe, bash, Git Bash, WSL, or any non-PowerShell shell:
STOP and report:
"Shell is not PowerShell. Please switch terminal to Windows PowerShell before continuing."

Forbidden shell workaround:
- Do NOT use powershell -Command from cmd.exe.
- Do NOT use pwsh -Command from cmd.exe.
- Do NOT wrap PowerShell commands inside any non-PowerShell shell.
- Do NOT adapt by using cmd syntax.
- Do NOT use curl.
- Do NOT use bash commands.
- Do NOT run hidden/background commands for build, git, API tests, or DB checks.

Before running project commands, confirm current directory:

Get-Location

If current directory is outside:

C:\Users\lieml\Desktop\Big Personal Web App\kost48surabaya-v3\kost48_full_frontend_backend_upgrade_bundle\final_bundle

STOP and report.

All API tests must use Invoke-RestMethod.

Protected endpoint format:

$token="PASTE_TOKEN_HERE"; Invoke-RestMethod -Method Get -Uri "http://localhost:3000/api/..." -Headers @{Authorization="Bearer $token"}

JSON POST/PATCH/PUT format:

$token="PASTE_TOKEN_HERE"; Invoke-RestMethod -Method Patch -Uri "http://localhost:3000/api/..." -Headers @{Authorization="Bearer $token"} -ContentType "application/json" -Body '{"field":"value"}'

Do not use placeholder URLs like ID_STAY.
If an ID is unknown, say:
"replace with a real numeric ID"
and give an example such as:
http://localhost:3000/api/stays/9/cancel

============================================================
WORK MODE RULES
============================================================

Use one mode only:
- PLAN: audit, explain, sequence, decide scope
- ACT: edit code, build, verify minimal result

Do not mix PLAN and ACT.

For PLAN:
- Do not edit files.
- Do not run build unless explicitly requested.
- Do not mutate database.
- Read only the allowed files.
- Stop after producing audit/plan report.

For ACT:
- Work on one vertical slice only.
- Do not open a broad scope.
- Do not rewrite the whole backend/frontend.
- Do not touch unrelated modules.
- Do not run long UAT unless the user explicitly asks for final UAT.
- Do not create test data unless the current task explicitly requires it.
- Do not mutate database for exploratory testing.
- Prefer code patch + build first.
- Mark manual/API tests as PENDING for final verification when appropriate.

Token and time economy:
- Do not repeat UAT that already passed unless the touched code affects that flow.
- Do not login repeatedly unless needed.
- Do not run broad endpoint sweeps after every small patch.
- For code batches: audit files → patch → build → short report.
- Large API/manual UAT should be reserved for final verification gates.

