============================================================
BATCH B1 MANUAL CHECK-IN BUSINESS AUTOMATION
============================================================

Status:
- NEXT P0.
- Not started yet.
- Must start with PLAN audit.
- Do NOT start with ACT.

Business problem:
Manual check-in currently can produce:
- tenant created,
- room OCCUPIED,
- stay ACTIVE,
- initial meter recorded,
but:
- initial invoice may remain DRAFT,
- portal user may not be auto-created,
- tenant may not be able to login portal,
- tenant may not see invoice,
- admin must remember extra manual steps.

B1 target:
Manual check-in completed should produce:
- Stay ACTIVE.
- Room OCCUPIED.
- Initial meter recorded.
- Initial invoice ISSUED.
- Portal user auto-created if tenant has email.
- If portal user is newly created, response returns temporary password once.
- Frontend CheckInWizard displays portal result and copy password button.
- If tenant email is missing, check-in still succeeds and portal status is clearly shown as unavailable.
- If portal already exists for the same tenant, check-in still succeeds with ALREADY_ACTIVE.
- If email belongs to another user/tenant, block with clear conflict before final side effects.

Portal auto-create statuses:
- MISSING_EMAIL: tenant.email is empty, skip portal creation, check-in succeeds.
- CREATED: tenant.email exists and no portal user exists, create TENANT user and return temporary password once.
- ALREADY_ACTIVE: portal user already exists for same tenant, no duplicate user, no error.
- CONFLICT: email is used by another user/tenant, block before final room/stay side effects.

B1 forbidden scope:
- Do not modify docs unless user explicitly asks.
- Do not change schema.
- Do not reset database.
- Do not touch production.
- Do not touch deposit settlement.
- Do not touch damage/penalty.
- Do not touch renewal.
- Do not touch final utility charge.
- Do not rewrite public booking.
- Do not touch urgency chip.
- Do not add KTP upload.
- Do not open large frontend/backend rewrite.

B1 PLAN audit allowed files to read:
- backend/src/modules/stays/stays.service.ts
- backend/src/modules/stays/stays.controller.ts
- backend/src/modules/stays/dto/**
- backend/src/modules/tenants/tenants.service.ts
- backend/src/modules/tenants/tenants.controller.ts
- backend/src/modules/tenants/dto/**
- backend/src/modules/users/users.service.ts
- backend/src/auth/auth.service.ts
- backend/prisma/schema.prisma
- frontend/src/pages/stays/CheckInWizard.tsx
- frontend/src/pages/stays/check-in-wizard/**
- frontend/src/api/stays.ts
- frontend/src/api/tenants.ts
- frontend/src/types/index.ts

B1 PLAN audit requirements:
1. Trace current POST /stays manual check-in flow.
2. Confirm invoice status created by StaysService.create(): DRAFT or ISSUED.
3. Confirm where invoice line RENT is created.
4. Confirm whether response currently returns enough data for frontend.
5. Trace existing tenant portal creation method.
6. Confirm how temporary password is generated and hashed.
7. Confirm whether portal creation can be reused safely from StaysService.create().
8. Identify logic needed for MISSING_EMAIL, CREATED, ALREADY_ACTIVE, CONFLICT.
9. Confirm how to avoid side effects if email conflict happens.
10. Propose minimal response DTO shape for CheckInWizard.
11. Propose minimal frontend success modal change.
12. List exact files for ACT.
13. Give backend/frontend build commands.
14. Give UAT checklist.

B1 PLAN stop condition:
- No code changes.
- No docs changes.
- No DB mutation.
- Stop after audit report.

B1 ACT can only start after user approves PLAN.

Likely B1 ACT files after PLAN approval:
- backend/src/modules/stays/stays.service.ts
- backend/src/modules/stays/stays.controller.ts only if response shape/controller typing needs adjustment
- backend/src/modules/tenants/tenants.service.ts only if portal helper must be reused or extracted
- frontend/src/pages/stays/CheckInWizard.tsx
- frontend/src/pages/stays/check-in-wizard/** only if success display is there
- frontend/src/api/stays.ts
- frontend/src/types/index.ts

B1 Definition of Done:
- Manual check-in creates Stay ACTIVE.
- Room becomes OCCUPIED.
- Initial meter is recorded.
- Initial invoice is ISSUED.
- Portal user is created if tenant has email and no existing portal user.
- Temporary password is returned once only when portal user is newly created.
- Frontend displays portal status and temporary password with copy button when CREATED.
- Missing email does not block check-in but displays portal unavailable.
- Existing portal for same tenant does not error.
- Email conflict blocks before final side effects.
- Backend build PASS.
- Frontend build PASS.
- Manual/API UAT performed before claiming PASS.

B1 UAT checklist:
1. Manual check-in tenant baru dengan email:
   - stay ACTIVE
   - room OCCUPIED
   - invoice ISSUED
   - portalEmail + temporaryPassword shown
   - copy password works
   - tenant can login portal
   - tenant sees current stay
   - tenant sees invoice ISSUED
2. Manual check-in tenant tanpa email:
   - check-in succeeds
   - portal status says unavailable/missing email
   - no portal user created
3. Manual check-in tenant existing with existing portal:
   - check-in succeeds
   - portal status ALREADY_ACTIVE
   - no duplicate user
4. Manual check-in with email used by another user/tenant:
   - check-in fails with clear conflict message
   - room status does not change
   - stay is not created

